            <ArticleTitle>Whole-Genome Sequence of the First Sequence Type 27 Brucella ceti Strain Isolated from European Waters.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">e00988-17</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1128/genomeA.00988-17</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Brucella spp. that cause marine brucellosis are becoming more important, as the disease appears to be more widespread than originally thought. Here, we report a whole and annotated genome sequence of Brucella ceti CRO350, a sequence type 27 strain isolated from a bottlenose dolphin carcass found in the Croatian part of the northern Adriatic Sea.</AbstractText>
